rn": 30, "text": "After Black's J3 (10.1 points lost, lead -25.6), White was about as far ahead as it got. Opus 5.5's J2 then lost 9.6 points, and the engine preferred G8."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "J5 was Opus 5.5's worst move, losing 15.4 points and moving the lead from -25.5 to -10.1. The engine preferred C6. White stayed ahead, but this one move gave away more than half of the margin."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py prints each group's liberties, count.py tallies stones and enclosed territory on a pasted board, and after.py applies one move the player names and shows the resulting captures and liberties. None of them loops over candidate moves, scores points, or plays a sequence forward, so they only inspect the current position or a single named move.", "stop": false}}